 "result": "All of this is in `src/tessel/views.py`.\n\n1. **`VerbView.__init_subclass__`** (165) runs when you subclass. It scans for `get`, `post` and the other names in `http_method_funcs`, and sets `cls.methods` to the matching uppercase verbs, such as `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`. It also merges in `methods` from base classes, and skips this if the class defines `methods` itself.\n2. **`View.to_view_func(name, ...)`** (86) is a classmethod that builds the plain view function.\n   - It creates a new instance per request, or reuses one if `init_every_request` is `False`.\n   - It calls `active_app.ensure_sync(self.run_view)(**kwargs)`.\n   - It applies any `decorators`.\n   - It attaches `view_class`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` to the function (129–134), so route registration picks up the allowed methods.\n3. **`VerbView.run_view`** (182) does the dispatch.\n   - It looks up `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`.\n   - `HEAD` falls back to `get` if there is no `head` handler.\n   - It calls the handler through `ensure_sync` with the URL arguments.\n\nYou register it with `app.attach_route_rule(\"/counter\", view_func=CounterAPI.to_view_func(\"counter\"))`.",
